            <ArticleTitle>Volar denervation and osteophyte resection to relieve volar CMC joint pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-16</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/23320885.2016.1278171</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>At mean 125.6 months, pain was reduced from mean of 8.7 to 0.67, p &lt; .001. Each of three patients, two of whom were musicians, returned to full professional ability. It is concluded that volar CMC joint denervation is a useful procedure, preserving joint function and relieving pain long-term.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
